-- Onboard ComedyTickets audit candidates with more than 4 upcoming events.
--
-- Source CSV: /private/tmp/comedytickets-candidates-with-counts.csv
-- Generated from rows where comedytickets_event_count > 4 after excluding
-- rows that already matched an existing club by normalized name or address.
-- ComedyTickets is an aggregator/ticketing surface, not a first-party club
-- site, so these are hidden club shells with no scraping_sources rows. They
-- preserve the venue identity for later first-party website/scraper onboarding
-- without routing users to ComedyTickets.
--
-- Idempotency: this migration also guards every insert against existing clubs
-- by normalized name and by normalized street+state at apply time.
--
-- 2026-07-07 (pre-apply review): added a same-city containment guard — a
-- candidate is also skipped when its normalized name contains (or is contained
-- by) an existing club's normalized name in the same city+state, with the
-- shorter side at least 8 normalized chars. This catches showtime variants
-- ("Tacoma Comedy Club - Downtown - 7PM"), rooms ("Comedy Mothership - Fat
-- Man"), and renames ("Big Laugh Comedy Club Fort Worth" vs the onboarded
-- "Big Laugh Comedy Club") that exact-equality misses, while keeping
-- legitimately distinct cross-city siblings (e.g. Helium Buffalo).

